<article class="env-corollary" id="B6AF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B6AF">Corollary <span data-tag="B6AF">5.2.8.13</span>.</a> Let $(S_ L, S_ R)$ be a factorization system on an $\infty $-category $\calC $. Then the collections of morphisms $S_ L$ and $S_ R$ contain all equivalences and are stable under composition. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Propositions <a href="/tag/94A7" data-tag="94A7">5.2.8.11</a> and <a href="/tag/CBA5" data-tag="CBA5">5.2.8.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>